From 1fb4095ee1e3336d1ce66518d76e22a88edc9c9d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kayori <noduhgamingxd@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 01:16:26 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 01/20] media: i2c: add OmniVision OV9726 sensor driver

Add a V4L2 sub-device driver and devicetree binding for the OmniVision
OV9726, a 1.3 megapixel sensor on one MIPI CSI-2 data lane (1296x808, 10
bit, 24 MHz clock).

The register settings come from the Android MSM camera driver for this
sensor (Copyright (c) 2011, The Linux Foundation, GPL v2); there is no
public datasheet. The Bayer order, analogue gain range, pixel rate and
link frequency are not documented there and are unverified: the pixel
rate and link frequency are derived from the table frame timing at an
assumed 30 fps.

Only exposure and analogue gain are adjustable; there is one mode.
